# =============================================================================
# matrix — `*` is a scalar operator, not the matrix product.
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • The matrix product is a glyph: `·` contracts the inner dimensions.
#   • `*` between two matrices is therefore a named decline, so the intent
#     (product or elementwise) is never guessed from the shapes.
#   • Elementwise pairing is `⊙`; `*` and `/` stay scalar scaling.
#
# See also: tensor, matrix, ·, ⊙
# =============================================================================

# `*` over two 2×2 matrices: the product glyph is `·`.
main {
    let matrix<f32, [2, 2]> a ← [[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]] ↦ matrix<f32, [2, 2]>
    let matrix<f32, [2, 2]> b ← a * a
    print b
}
